[2026-03-14T23:23:39.844Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FHX4jBxhUGjPERnWP6SxEj","type":"tool_result","content":"191:- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n208:#### Test: Sidebar Labels link navigates correctly\n210:- **Action**: User clicks \"Labels\" in the workspace section\n211:- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/labels`.\n249:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is fully expanded showing labels and icons\n251:- **Expected**: The sidebar collapses to icon-only mode. Navigation items show only their icons without text labels. The sidebar width is significantly reduced. The main content area expands to fill the freed space.\n256:- **Expected**: The sidebar expands back to full width showing both icons and text labels. The main content area shrinks accordingly.\n279:- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n373:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee avatar, due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n374:- **Expected**: The issue row displays: High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\", title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n405:#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n406:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Frontend\" (blue)\n407:- **Expected**: Both labels are shown as small colored badges in the issue row, each with the label's color and name text.\n422:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project\n423:- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, or project. Only the present fields (priority, identifier, title, status, assignee) are shown.\n427:#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Priority, and Label filters\n429:- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Priority\" dropdown, and \"Label\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a multi-select dropdown.\n456:#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n457:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n458:- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n459:- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n461:#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n462:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n463:- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n464:- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n467:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n468:- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n469:- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (it matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n484:- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Status and Label filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n601:- **Expected**: The page displays a header with the team name \"Engineering\" and an \"Issues\" label. A \"New Issue\" button is visible in the header area.\n616:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee \"Jane Doe\" (with avatar), due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n617:- **Expected**: The issue row displays: a checkbox for bulk selection (unchecked), High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\" with team prefix, title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n658:#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n659:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Frontend\" (blue)\n660:- **Expected**: Both labels are shown as small colored badges in the issue row, each with the label's color and name text.\n667:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-43 has no labels, no due date, no project, no assignee\n668:- **Expected**: The issue row does not show empty placeholders for labels, due date, project, or assignee. Only the present fields (checkbox, priority, identifier, title, status) are shown.\n708:- **Expected**: A bulk action toolbar appears showing the selection count (\"1 selected\") and action buttons for: Status change, Priority change, Assignee change, and Label change.\n730:#### Test: Bulk label change updates all selected issues\n731:- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, ENG-42 (no labels) and ENG-43 (label \"Bug\") are selected","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4xaMBJpXq61wd3VDy2BUs","session_id":"2c440e31-04a9-4252-9689-26512ba806f5","uuid":"eaec2665-0756-4cae-8248-e7972cb6f3a9"}
